WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.369
-On your marks, get set, go!

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:04.504
-Go, Winnie,
go, Winnie, go, Winnie.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.105
Go, Winnie, go, Winnie,
go, Winnie.

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:07.540
-Careful!
-Yes, you got to go.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.309
Franny, go! You can go!
-I did it!

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:13.646
-Go, Franny, go, go, go, go!
-Go! Slide on in!

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:14.781
-Here I come!

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:17.016
-Franny, don't let Daddy
beat you!

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.519
-[ Screams ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:22.188
-...Franny!
-Franny!

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:25.625
-I'll get you next time.
Let's start the show.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.793
♪♪

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.428
-♪ We in the house ♪

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:29.895
♪ Come on ♪

00:00:29.895 --> 00:00:33.233
-Tonight join Jimmy
and his guests --

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.135
Queen Latifah...

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:37.003
Pete Davidson and Judd Apatow...

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:39.305
musical guest James Taylor...

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.374
and the legendary Roots crew.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.376
It's "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.177
-♪ We in the house, y'all ♪

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:48.248
-And now here's Jimmy.

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.482
-Hey, everybody.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.717
Welcome to "Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:53.719
I want to thank @AlexPresley-

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.922
on TikTok
for that back slide race.

00:00:56.922 --> 00:00:59.091
We've been doing it, and
it's really fun at the house.

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:01.460
All right.
Let's do tonight's monologue.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.731
-Wind me up, barber!

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:08.101
It's time for the monologue!

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.103
-Hey, guys.
This weekend is Mother's Day.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.071
But because of the pandemic,

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:15.875
Hooters isn't offering
their annual free meal for Mom.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.210
I'm sorry, honey.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.947
Kids and I will
try to make it up to you.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:23.616
We'll make your day special
still. Don't worry.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:26.252
Well, it's our eighth week
of quarantine,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.886
and I heard that some people

00:01:27.886 --> 00:01:30.823
are trying to relax by
turning their homes into spas.

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.493
Yeah, you just lie facedown,
turn on some soothing music,

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.127
then your kids jump on your back

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:37.730
until you turn on a movie
for them.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.533
Listen to this. Disney is now
offering the Disney bundle --

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:43.436
Gary. Gary, get out of there.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.207
That's --
What were you doing in there?

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.411
-Looking for something
to roll in again.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.745
-Yeah.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.348
Gary might have caught
some fox disease or something.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.650
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:01.754
-Gary, what are you even doing?

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.190
Maybe you're just an inside dog.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.827
Gary? Gary.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.662
You seem concerned.
Listen to this.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.964
Disney is now offering
the Disney bundle

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:15.901
which includes
Hulu, ESPN+, and Disney+

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.903
for $12.99 a month.

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:22.074
And this is cool -- for an
extra $5, you can own Disney.

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:23.409
Well, this isn't good.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.944
I read that Hawaii authorities

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.845
have been arresting
rogue tourists

00:02:26.845 --> 00:02:30.216
who are not abiding to
the state's quarantine orders.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.885
Also I'm 99% sure
that "Rogue Tourist"

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:36.322
is a straight-to-DVD movie
starring Liam Neeson.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:40.827
[As Neeson]
"I'm the rogue tourist.

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:45.465
I've got one grass skirt,
two bowls of poi.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:48.167
Race you to the gift shop."

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:52.571
Check this out. The first sample
of Kanye's Yeezy 451 sneakers

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:54.073
have been released.

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.943
Take a look at these things.
Huh.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.879
They look like
they're whispering, "Water."

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.315
[ Chuckles ]

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.983
It's the only shoe
where they ask

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:07.686
if you want it
in a cup or a cone.

00:03:07.686 --> 00:03:10.957
I saw a new study that says
raptors may have hunted solo

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.893
and not in packs
like in "Jurassic Park."

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:17.530
So I guess the 1993 movie
about a totally safe

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:21.167
dinosaur theme park
isn't historically accurate.

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:27.440
Gotcha! Ha ha!

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.941
And finally, this is incredible.

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:30.576
A 14-year-old
high-school graduate

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:33.612
has been accepted into
eight California Universities.

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:35.648
When I heard that, my first
thought was, "Damn, I got to

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.616
transfer my kids
into THAT homeschool."

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:39.519
Guys, that is our monologue
right there.

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.486
Thank you very much. What a show
we have for you tonight.

00:03:41.486 --> 00:03:43.256
Queen Latifah is here.

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:45.858
Judd Apatow,
Pete Davidson are here.

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:48.961
And we got great music
from James Taylor.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.497
The one and only James Taylor.
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:55.435
He's doing "Close Your Eyes"
with his wife and his son.

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:57.603
I know. I was
thinking about jumping in

00:03:57.603 --> 00:03:59.739
and seeing if I could get --
Maybe we'll do a song.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.874
"Close Your..."
That's going to be just --

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:04.877
It's just going to be beautiful.
I love him so much.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:08.680
I love the whole fam.
I'm so happy they're here.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.683
Guys, it's time for "Hashtags."

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.752
♪♪

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:15.487
♪ Hashtags ♪

00:04:15.487 --> 00:04:17.390
-Hey, guys,
it's time for "Hashtags."

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.927
The hashtags today are
#QuarantineMomQuotes.

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:23.562
These are quotes from your mom
made during the quarantine,

00:04:23.562 --> 00:04:25.498
because Mother's Day
is coming up.

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:29.035 line:0%
So here we go. Our first one
here is from @trixsyoyoforreal.

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:31.904 line:0%
They say, "When my mom goes on
her daily walk, she always says,

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:34.240 line:0%
'If something happens to me,
call me.'"

00:04:37.342 --> 00:04:41.447 line:0%
This one's from @quarantineq14.

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:44.917 line:0%
She says, "Mom --
Aunt Cheryl wants to Vroom.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.418 line:0%
You have to show me
how to do it.

00:04:46.418 --> 00:04:48.421 line:0%
ME --
Mom, do you mean Zoom?

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:50.322 line:0%
Mom -- No. Vroom."

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:52.357 line:0%
[ Laughs ]

00:04:52.357 --> 00:04:53.926 line:0%
